// ===================== PROLOGUE: T-MINUS =====================

=== prologue ===
# scene: P.1 Launch Day
# bg: BG01
# ambient: synth
YOU (V.O.): Launch day. Years of training, and my heart is still racing.
# zoom: figurine
YOU (V.O.): Mimi painted the visor gold. She says it's so astronauts can look at the sun without squinting.
# zoom: off
# call: happy
MIMI: You're doing your "I'm fine" face.
YOU: This is my regular face.
MIMI: Rules. One: come home. Two: send pictures. Three: bring me a moon rock.
YOU: Moon rocks go to the scientists, so everyone can learn from them. But I get one small bag for personal things. Your astronaut is in it.
# call: curious
MIMI: Why is the visor really gold?
YOU: A very thin layer of real gold bounces the Sun's heat away. You were half right. # ref_needed: gold visor
MIMI: Why do you have to live up there? Why not just visit?
YOU: To find out if people can. Everything we decide gets written down, so the next crew knows more than we did.
# call: end
TITLE: Four astronauts. One outpost on the Moon's south pole. Every danger in this game comes from real NASA data.
-> ch1
